<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harihara I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1336–1356</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harihara">Harihara</a> I was the founder, with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukka-raya-i">Bukka I</a>, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a> and its first ruling house, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangama-dynasty">Sangama dynasty</a>. Having probably served the Kampili or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> rulers, the brothers established their kingdom on the Tungabhadra around 1336 as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a> authority in the south collapsed, and Harihara extended his rule over much of the former Hoysala lands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harihara-i.jpg" alt="Harihara I" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HariHara_I_coin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
